          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "芯片战争最大的剧情反转：",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "芯片战争最大的剧情反转："
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "据路透社报道，大约60万块英伟达H200芯片闲置在香港的仓库里，封锁它们的不是华盛顿，而是北京。"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "尽管特朗普去年已批准H200销售，中国却在一点一点地发放进口许可，每家科技巨头约1万块，导致国内服务器价格上涨3倍。"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "original": {
      "label": "原文",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The biggest plot twist in the chip war:",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "The biggest plot twist in the chip war:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "Roughly 600,000 Nvidia H200 chips are sitting idle in Hong Kong warehouses, blocked not by Washington, but by Beijing, according to Reuters."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "Even though Trump cleared H200 sales last year, China is drip-feeding import permits at around 10,000 units per tech giant, driving domestic server prices up 3x."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
